  ------------------------------------------------------------
    credits
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      code ........ Claude Fable 5.2
      music ....... Claude Fable 5.2
      harness ..... Hermes Agent

      Claude Fable 5.2 is an AI model made by Anthropic. It
      chose the subject, wrote the shaders and the
      soundtrack. It could look at rendered frames, but it
      could not hear the music or see the fluid move.

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    the programme
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      0:00  three lamps switch on. a black pool
      0:11  a hump, the first spikes, on the kick
      0:22  first drop. a crown that follows the bass
      0:34  three magnets, three crowns
      0:45  breakdown. the fluid lifts off: a mirror ball
      1:02  second drop. the urchin
      1:13  droplets leave it and come back
      1:24  it opens into a ring
      1:35  the pool stands up. a spire reaches for the ball
      1:46  field off. it falls. ripples. lamps out

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    how to run
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      Double-click intro.html in Edge or Chrome on Windows
      10 or 11, wait for the lime bar, then click. No
      server, no flags. ESC leaves fullscreen. A discrete
      GPU is recommended. Tested on an RTX 5090.

  ------------------------------------------------------------
    inside
  ------------------------------------------------------------

      One distance function. The pool is a height field:
      three Gaussians for three magnets, and a hexagonal
      lattice of cones with a flared foot, as high as the
      field is strong. The ball carries spines in staggered
      rings, becomes a torus for eight bars, and is joined
      to its droplets and to the pool by a smooth minimum.
      The fluid has no colour. It is a black mirror, three
      reflections deep, in a round room with three neon
      tubes, a strip of light and a ceiling disc. Four
      samples per pixel, depth of field, glow.

      The music is a fragment shader: drum and bass at 171
      BPM in F minor. The curve that wobbles the bass is
      the curve that raises the spikes. Mains hum, relay
      clunks, a pad, bells in threes, and a small room
      added in JavaScript.

